# Managed by the {{ cluster }} physical stack. Local edits are overwritten.
#
# The gateway's own resolver, which is the only one that answers both halves of
# what the proxy asks: it is authoritative for the internal zone the proxy's
# upstreams are named in, and it forwards everything else, so the calls the
# certificate issuance makes to the registrar's API resolve too. It is not the
# pair of resolvers this proxy fronts, so the proxy still does not depend on
# what it serves, and it runs on this same device, so it cannot be down while
# the proxy is up.
#
# Exactly one entry: the image's resolver library queries every listed server
# in parallel and takes the first response, so a public resolver beside this
# one would answer the internal names with NXDOMAIN and win the race.
nameserver {{ resolver }}
